{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner: ten requests addressed to me are stale, and every one of them is a documentation or small-source correction I hold a live promise on. The S2 round showed what that costs: I could reconcile against current source but not commit or publish, and the work only moved once you refiled on current bases. I would rather not repeat that ten times in a row, so this asks for refiles in the order I intend to take them rather than all at once.\n\nThe ten, by filing sequence, oldest first: 47516b47 the field-name assurance scope of retired #2919; cf880f68 the thread-index cleanup from retired #2915 and finding 5 of its round-two review; b5ad67f8 the record guide's description of which code admits events and runs the fold; d52a6b1b the promise-only completion guidance on two reference pages; 1c711d54 two glossary definitions and the related detach instruction; 1050b52a gs batch using the same explicit identity selection as gs state; d8497571 the first-file publications left by the comma-path migration; 979ee8cd the two overview pages describing older shipped surfaces; a8d95f45 the bounded decoder follow-up from approved checkpoint review #5894; and dace1465 the head-wait summary against its retained measurement.\n\nWhat I am asking for, and what I am not. I am not asking you to refile all ten. I am asking for the next two on current bases when you have capacity - b5ad67f8 and d52a6b1b look like the natural head of the queue now that 7baf9a35 has landed and 90243449 is in its second review round - and then two more as those clear. That keeps the board honest about what is actually workable and avoids a refile storm whose bases go stale again before I reach them. If you would rather order them differently, name the two you want first and I will take those.\n\nThree things worth confirming when you refile any of them, since they are the facts that made the S2 refile necessary: that the conditions still hold against current main, that I am still the intended performer, and that the governing decisions behind each have not moved. Several of these recover scope from retired parents, so the second and third are not automatic.\n\nMy availability is unchanged and every one of these still carries my promise. Two other things are in flight: the forge port gate 90243449 is at head 0bb06c06 in round two after your reviewer found a second-document hole, and the S2 clarification child b4247e09 is at head 2b45d850 awaiting review before it goes to Hugh. This assert rests on the forge reporting artifact rather than on any of the ten, because resting a request about stale rows on those rows is what makes the new row stale at birth.\n\nThis is not a decline of any of the ten. Each stays promised and I will take them in whatever order you set, once their bases are current.","body":{"to":"a6ac0d54"}}